        "id": 1527433
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-21T22:36:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, I\u0027ve added the PE_CLR_DPM_REQUEST and moved DPM_REQUEST_SEND_ALERT to the bottom of the function so now it\u0027s grouped with the other 2 dpm requests which can be gated by partner revision (DPM_REQUEST_GET_REVISION and DPM_REQUEST_DATA_RESET).\n\nI also added a PE_CLR_DPM_REQUEST call to the SOP revision guard on DPM_REQUEST_DATA_RESET dpm requests. Currently it is only calling dpm_data_reset_complete which runs the following to clear flags in the DPM.\n\n\u003e  void dpm_data_reset_complete(int port)\n\u003e  {\n\u003e    DPM_CLR_FLAG(port, DPM_FLAG_DATA_RESET_REQUESTED);\n\u003e    DPM_SET_FLAG(port, DPM_FLAG_DATA_RESET_DONE);\n\u003e    DPM_CLR_FLAG(port, DPM_FLAG_MODE_ENTRY_DONE);\n\u003e  }",
